    "Two-jig workflow: put the PCB bottom side up in the placement jig, fit the parts, put this holding jig on top (pockets down), turn the stack over, lift off the placement jig and solder from above.",
    "Fit check (89 parts, their 3D shapes): nothing touches on the way in; all 1 hand-soldered parts touch their pockets as the board lands on the support (within 0.01 mm) and are held on all four sides (0.23 to 0.23 mm of play); held by the part beside it, too close for a jig wall between them: J9 -x against C8 (0.19 mm), J9 -y against C8 (0.19 mm); the holding jig closes over the placement jig without touching it. Estimated (box) shapes: J1, J9, JP1.",
